  "id": "memdb-file-storage-locking-and-mapping",
  "title": "Memdb shared/private storage, file methods, locking, and mapping",
  "status": "inventoried",
  "admission_ready": false,
  "scope": {
    "rationale": "These active memdb.c methods own shared-versus-private store creation and last-close destruction, contiguous doubled-capacity byte I/O, rollback-only truncation/sync, reader/writer locks, fetch behavior, file controls, ABI method tails, access, and pathname handling. The dedicated native memdb owner now follows these target-profile traces. The source MemStore/MemFile/MemFS representations, method tables, selected mutex helpers, delegated VFS services, and memdb identity predicate are also assigned here.",
